# Runtime assets are generated, checksum-verified artefacts. Git must never rewrite their bytes.
#
# With the default core.autocrlf=true on Windows, checkout converted the trailing newline of
# tile-index.json from LF to CRLF. That added a single byte, so its SHA-256 no longer matched the
# indexSha256 declared in tiles.json, OfflineTiles.prepare() failed its integrity check, and the
# Delhi & NCR offline map reported "The active map could not be opened" on every Windows clone.
# Twelve assets were affected the same way, including wmm2025.wmm, the magnetic-model coefficients
# GeographicLib parses for heading initialisation.
#
# The integrity checks were right; the bytes reaching them were wrong. Marking the whole asset tree
# binary is what keeps a verified artefact byte-identical from build machine to device.
android/app/src/main/assets/** -text

# Map packs and model bundles are verified the same way wherever they are staged.
*.setumap  -text
*.pbf      -text
*.mbtiles  -text
*.wmm      -text
*.wmm.cof  -text

# Large generated graph, stored out of line.
android/app/src/main/assets/regions/delhi/roads.bin.gzip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
